{{also|Eagle}}
==English==
{{rfquote|en}}
[[File:Haliaeetus leucocephalus in flight over KSC.jpg|thumb|[[bald eagle|Bald eagle]] ({{taxfmt|Haliaeetus leucocephalus|species}})]]
[[File:Eagles in heraldry - collage of arms of Germany Poland Mexico and Egypt.png|thumb|The coats of arms of Germany, Poland, Mexico and Egypt (among others) depict eagles in various colors and styles.]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|egle}}, from {{der|en|xno|egle}}, from {{der|en|fro|aigle}}, from {{der|en|la|aquila}}. Displaced native {{cog|enm|earn|ern, earn, arn}}, from {{cog|ang|earn|t=eagle}}. More at {{m|en|erne}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈiːɡəl/|[ˈɪi̯ɡəl]|~|[ˈɪi̯ɡl̩]}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-eagle.wav|a=Southern England}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-eagle.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːɡəl|s=2}}
* {{hyph|en|ea|gle}}
* {{hmp|en|egal}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q2092297}}Any of several large carnivorous and [[carrion]]-eating [[bird]]s in the family {{taxfmt|Accipitridae|family}}, having a powerful [[hooked]] [[bill]] and [[keen]] [[vision]].
#: {{syn|en|erne|broadwing}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=2017|artist=w:Arch Enemy|title={{w|Will to Power (Arch Enemy album)|The '''Eagle''' Flies Alone}}
|passage=I, I go my own way<br/>I swim against the stream<br/>Forever I will fight the pοwers that be<br/>The '''eagle''' flies alone}}
# {{lb|en|US|numismatics|historical|nocat=y}} A [[gold]] [[coin]] with a face value of ten dollars, formerly used in the United States.
# {{lb|en|historical|numismatics|nocat=y}} A 13th-[[century]] [[coin]] [[mint]]ed in [[Europe]] and [[circulate]]d in [[England]] as a [[debase]]d [[sterling]] [[silver]] [[penny]], [[outlaw]]ed under {{w|Edward I of England}}.
# {{lb|en|golf}} A score of [[two]] [[under par]] for a [[hole]].
#: {{ux|en|I got an '''eagle''' in the third hole.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=w:San Francisco Chronicle|title=Warriors’ Steph Curry commits to play in Lake Tahoe golf tournament|date=May 27 2025|author=Ron Kroichick|url=https://www.sfchronicle.com/sports/warriors/article/steph-curry-golf-tahoe-20344474.php
|text=His '''eagle''' on the 54th and final hole, a par-5, vaulted him to a dramatic victory in the marquee celebrity golf tournament.}}

