===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*dʰewh₂-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|dust}}, {{m|enm|doust}}, from {{inh|en|ang|dūst||dust, dried earth reduced to powder; other dry material reduced to powder}}, from the fusion of {{inh|en|gem-pro|*dustą||dust}} and {{m|gem-pro|*dunstą||mist, dust, evaporation}}, both from {{der|en|ine-pro|*dʰewh₂-||to smoke, raise dust}}.

Cognate with {{cog|sco|dust}}, {{m|sco|dist||dust}}, {{cog|nl|duist||pollen, dust}} and {{m|nl|dons||down, fuzz}}, {{cog|de|Dust||dust}} and {{m|de|Dunst||haze}}, {{cog|sv|dust||dust}}, {{cog|is|dust||dust}}, {{cog|la|fūmus||smoke, steam}}. Also related to {{cog|sv|dun||down, fluff}}, {{cog|is|dúnn||down, fluff}}. See {{l|en|down}}.

