===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# [[fine|Fine]] [[particle]]s.
## {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[fine|Fine]], [[dry]] [[particle]]s of [[matter]] found in the air and [[cover]]ing the [[surface]] of [[object]]s, typically [[consist]]ing of [[soil]] [[lift]]ed up by the wind, [[pollen]], [[hair]], [[fiber]] [[debris]], dead [[skin cell]]s, etc.
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022 September 7|title=East-West track laying heads westwards|journal=RAIL|issue=965|page=37, photo caption|text=There is so much '''dust''' released during the process of laying ballast that the trackside operator wears a full face mask with respirator.}}
## {{lb|en|uncountable}} Any [[substance]] [[reduce]]d to fine particles; [[powder]].
## {{lb|en|uncountable|astronomy}} [[submicron|Submicron]] particles in [[outer space]], largely [[silicate|silicates]] and [[carbon]] [[compound]]s, that [[contribute]] greatly to [[extinction]] at [[visible]] [[wavelength]]s.
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=June 29, 2020|journal=BBC News|titleurl=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/science-environment-53218658|title=Betelgeuse: Nearby ‘supernova’ star’s dimming explained|author=Paun Rincon|passage=Astronomers have previously considered that '''dust''' produced by the star was obscuring it, causing the steep decline in brightness.}}
## {{lb|en|uncountable|occupational health}} [[disintegration|Disintegration]] of a [[solid]], like [[silica]].
## {{lb|en|uncountable|Australia|slang|dated}} [[flour|Flour]].
## {{lb|en|countable|obsolete}} A single fine, dry particle of earth or other material; [[grain]] of dust.
##* {{RQ:Shakespeare Richard 2|act=II|scene=iii|passage=to touch a '''dust''' of England’s ground}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} The act of [[clean]]ing by dusting.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2010|author=Joan Busfield; Michael Paddon|title=Thinking About Children: Sociology and Fertility in Post-War England|page=150
|passage={{...}}once they start school, I mean you can do a room out one day, the next day it only needs a '''dust''', doesn’t it?}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} The act of [[sprinkle|sprinkling]] dust, or a sprinkle of dust itself.
# {{lb|en|poetic}} [[earth|Earth]], [[ground]], [[soil]], [[sediment]].
#* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam|XXXV|54|But I should turn mine ears and hear<br>The moanings of the homeless sea,<br>⁠The sound of streams that swift or slow<br>⁠Draw down Æonian hills, and sow<br>The '''dust''' of continents to be; {{...}}}}
# The earth as the [[resting place]] of the [[dead]].
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Job|7|21|passage=For now shall I sleep in the '''dust'''.}}
# The [[earthly]] [[remains]] of [[body|bodies]] once [[alive]]; the remains of the [[human]] [[body]].
#* {{RQ:Tennyson Poems 1842|volume=II|poem=St. Simeon Stylites|page=62|passage=For I will leave my relics in your land, / And you may carve a shrine about my '''dust''', / And burn a fragrant lamp before my bones, / When I am gather’d to the glorious saints.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} The [[substance]] of the human body or [[mortal]] [[frame]].
# {{lb|en|figurative}} Something [[worthless]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare King John|act=III|scene=i|passage=And by the merit of vile gold, dross, '''dust'''.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} A [[low]] or [[mean]] [[condition]].
#* {{RQ:King James Version|1 Samuel|2|8|passage=[God] raiseth up the poor out of the '''dust'''.}}
# {{lb|en|Britain|colloquial}} [[rubbish|Rubbish]], [[garbage]], [[refuse]].
# {{lb|en|slang|dated}} [[cash]]; [[money]] (in reference to [[gold dust]]).
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1852|author=George Colvocoresses|title=Four Years in a Government Exploring Expedition|passage=‘And what do you ask for it?’ ‘Fifteen thousand dollars.’ ‘I’ll take it.’ ‘Then down with the '''dust'''.’}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[cloud]] of dust.
# {{lb|en|countable|figurative}} A [[tumult]], [[disturbance]], [[commotion]], [[uproar]].
#: {{ux|en|to raise, or kick up, a '''dust'''}}
# {{lb|en|countable|colloquial}} A [[fight]] or [[row]].
# {{lb|en|countable|mathematics}} A totally [[disconnected]] [[set]] of [[point]]s with a [[fractal]] structure.
# {{lb|en|cryptocurrency}} Tiny amounts of [[cryptocurrency]] left over after a [[transaction]] due to [[rounding error]].

